## Proposed Solution for Issue #15

### Root Cause Analysis & Fix
The root cause was that the scan‑result formatter truncated the last entry when the payload contained a line‑break, because it split on a hard‑coded "\n\n" delimiter and then dropped the final chunk. The fix normalises line endings, uses a robust regex to capture each markdown bullet, and ensures all entries are included before rendering the final report.

### Proposed Code Patch
```
--- a/src/scanFormatter.js
+++ b/src/scanFormatter.js
@@
-function formatResults(raw) {
-  // NOTE: raw data is separated by double newlines; the last chunk may be empty
-  const chunks = raw.split('\n\n');
-  const items = chunks.slice(0, -1).map(parseChunk);
-  return renderReport(items);
-}
+function formatResults(raw) {
+  // Normalize line endings to avoid platform‑specific splits
+  const normalized = raw.replace(/\r\n/g, '\n');
+  // Each bounty entry starts with a markdown header like "#### n. [title]"
+  // Use a global regex to capture all entries, including the final one
+  const entryRegex = /####\s+\d+\.\s+\[.*?\][\s\S]*?(?=\n####\s+\d+\.\s+\[|$)/g;
+  const matches = normalized.match(entryRegex) || [];
+  const items = matches.map(parseChunk);
+  return renderReport(items);
+}
*** End of File ***
```

