## Proposed Solution for Issue #11

### Root Cause Analysis & Fix
The gain/loss logic compared the threshold values as strings, causing lexical rather than numeric comparison which broke the route‑selection when the thresholds crossed 9 (e.g., "10" < "9" evaluates true). Converting the inputs to numbers before the comparison fixes the threshold handling and restores correct route selection.

